\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces  Comparison of signal gain, noise gain, and phase shift of causal numerical differentiation methods on a noisy $1$~Hz input signal sampled at $200$~Hz. Each method implements smoothing according to a given cutoff frequency to supress the ampliciation of noise. The DoG method provides the lowest noise gain across all cutoff frequencies, but also a considerable phase shift. }}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bode}{{4}{4}{}{}{}}
